    description: "Classify the 4 pending_classification edge types — resolver_implements, resolver_for_type, openapi_implements, implements_rpc (the \"resolver/OpenAPI/RPC family\"; edge_types.py:344-346 says the family \"awaits its own audit\"). Every OTHER family's per-family audit exists and is done (dispatch WI-kofuh-fovar, publish WI-kusif-gamup, IPC WI-fugun-butil); this family's audit was never filed — a gap in the ADR-0023 per-family audit set (OQ4 pattern).\n\nWORK: per-family audit deciding, for EACH of the 4, a CANONICAL / FOLD / DEPRECATE verdict via ADR-0024's four leakage tests (property-derivability, apex/peer overloading, construct-vs-relationship, mechanism-vs-category). Working hypothesis (NOT a conclusion): several are likely CANONICAL — a GraphQL resolver-for-type binding and an RPC \"implements\" are arguably genuinely distinct relationships, not endpoint leakage — but the verdict must come from the tests, not the hypothesis. Outcome flows into the EDGE_TYPES axis assignment (move each of the 4 to `relationship` if CANONICAL, or `endpoint_shape` + a fold target if FOLD). File as docs/audits/<NN>-<topic>.md per the audit-findings convention, NOT a new ADR.\n\nNOT a blocker for WI-pusuv: WI-pusuv's 4 pending_classification types are already outside its endpoint_shape census blocker (the census gate is the 23 endpoint_shape in-scope types, not the pending_classification 4). Parent: the endpoint_shape fold-tail umbrella."  # 4173
